disappoint the team"},{"id":"C","text":"discover the truth"},{"id":"D","text":"submit the homework"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Use the **whole verb + particle**, and check its meaning against the object.","explanation":"Here **let down** means **disappoint the team**. Learn this verb–particle combination as a unit.","keywords":["phrasal-meaning"],"skill":"phrasal-meaning","contextKey":"phrasal-verbs-49","fingerprint":"bda01647e02ebdcedd5ee6c379161cc6beb366bb811bdd278a9252b973d9e409","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-phrasal-order"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Use the **whole verb + particle**, and check its meaning against the object.","Here **let down** means **disappoint the team**. Learn this verb–particle combination as a unit.","Choose **disappoint the team**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"That would describe “hand out the leaflets”, not the expression used here.","B":"Here **let down** means **disappoint the team**. Learn this verb–particle combination as a unit.","C":"That would describe “find out the truth”, not the expression used here.","D":"That would describe “hand in the homework”, not the expression used here."}}},{"id":"86306313-e309-5a8b-a492-abe1e24a4252","topicSlug":"phrasal-verbs","level":"B2","prompt":"Replace “the team” with “it” in this separable phrasal verb: “Please let down the team.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"let down it"},{"id":"B","text":"it let down"},{"id":"C","text":"let it to down"},{"id":"D","text":"let it down"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The object is now a **pronoun**, so place it **in the middle**.","explanation":"An object pronoun goes **between the verb and particle**: let it down.","keywords":["pronoun-placement"],"skill":"pronoun-placement","contextKey":"phrasal-verbs-49","fingerprint":"fce6e6199d7dfd247294b6cad655f9c82